  "body": "## Summary\n\nThe v63 fixture now omits `break_through_from`, which first appeared in v68.\nThe test checks the loaded `BreakThroughFrom::Tip` and the stated `break_through: 0.0`.\nIt checks the saved `\"tip\"` reference, all other parameters, and a byte-stable current-format round trip.\nThe expected JSON now includes the migrated reference, not only a new version.\n\nThis changes one existing test and its decision note. Production code does not change.\n\n## Verification\n\nThese checks passed on the submitted tree:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate test a_v63_break_through_file_steps_up_without_losing_the_stated_limit --crate camcraft-app --binary sketch_project --exact`\n- `cargo xtask gate test v65_preserves_cutting_steps_and_loads_v63_break_through_and_v62_defaults --crate camcraft-app --binary break_through --exact`\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` selected and ran the changed fixture: one step, zero failures.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`\n- `git diff --check`\n\nThe original fixture passed before this coverage correction, as expected.\nA temporary mutation made the missing-key migration choose `FullDiameter` instead of `Tip`.\nThe corrected fixture failed at its explicit Tip assertion while the zero allowance stayed unchanged.\nThe mutation was fully restored. The quick gate and neighboring migration test then passed again.\n\n## Limits\n\nLight lane: Not run. The bounded test-only scope excludes release-mode and app-wide suites, despite the general light-lane policy.\nNo toolpath or post code changed, so the example catalog suites were not run.\nNo GUI, full-workspace, heavy, release, or physical-machine checks were run.\nHosted check status is reported separately; absent checks are not a green CI result.\n\nEffort: low\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #2633\n",
